{
  "_id": "fhSubTriBurn0001",
  "name": "Triple-Burn",
  "type": "consumable",
  "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
  "folder": "fhSubModern00001",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>An aerosolized blend of three commercial stimulants and a fourth ingredient the lab denies, sold in dented inhalers from gas-station back rooms. Three sharp puffs are tradition; two will do; four ends a career.</p><p><strong><em>Desired effects on use.</em></strong> For 1 hour you have advantage on initiative rolls and on Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks.</p><p><strong><em>On use, save against addiction.</em></strong> Make a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, you gain the Addicted condition from Triple-Burn (see below).</p><p><strong><em>Addicted from Triple-Burn.</em></strong> While you have this Addicted condition, you are also Poisoned and have disadvantage on Charisma checks (you talk too fast and finish other people's sentences badly).</p><p><strong><em>Withdrawal.</em></strong> At the end of each Long Rest while addicted, you either take another dose or abstain. If you abstain, make a DC 11 Wisdom check to resist the craving; on a failure, you give in and take a dose. On a success, you go into withdrawal for 1 day, or half that if you succeed on a DC 13 Constitution saving throw. If you have no doses left, skip the Wisdom check. While in withdrawal you take a -2 penalty to all ability checks and saving throws and have disadvantage on initiative rolls. Abstaining then takes only the Wisdom check, and taking any dose ends the withdrawal but not the addiction. When the withdrawal ends, so does the addiction.</p><p><strong><em>Overdose.</em></strong> If you take a dose while still under its effects, or once your tolerance is at its limit, there is a 15% chance you overdose: you take 2d6 poison damage and have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute.</p><p><strong><em>Dosing others.</em></strong> As an action, you can blow a dose into the face of a creature within 5 feet. If the creature fails a DC 13 Constitution saving throw, it is dosed.</p><p><em>Requires ready paraphernalia that applies to inhaled substances, such as Rolling Papers or a Calibrated Inhaler.</em></p>"
    },
